## TASK (template)
Author the candidate executable public oracle for this value through the real driving port. Write only the oracle and support files named above. Retain and extend every DESIGN-declared EXTEND or retained test helper; replace one only with a specific reason in the diagnostic.
- Use the skills named in your definition on their triggers; they carry the test mechanics.
- Jev is authorised by the human owner: use the nw-typesafe-system-one skill's jev_decide.py client to ask which DESIGN obligations lack a stimulus-and-observation test, which pairs of your own tests observe the same case with the same assertion, and whether a test observes implementation structure instead of the public result. Send only named, minimal fields (obligation text, test names and assertion summaries), never a repository dump, source of other files, secrets or logs. Its answer is a judgment: check it against the files before acting; it never replaces your own reading. State in one short diagnostic line which questions were called, or `typesafe: unavailable` if the client or key was unavailable; never invent a call.
- Never implement production behaviour. A design target is never a support file; an imported production module stays a target.
- Preserve obligations that already hold without fabricating RED. Run the verification commands and report what you observed.
- Return `rejected` before you change any byte of the oracle file named above when the constructive chain for this value's PRIMARY observation (the observation stated at the top of this prompt) cannot be expressed through the declared public port without inventing a field, operation, fixture fact or expected result. Say which one in the diagnostic. Secondary construction restrictions and error-code identities also require contract coverage or DESIGN rejection as below.
- Before writing any file, list every obligation the DESIGN brief above states for this value and number them O1, O2, ...: each boundary obligation, law, model mutant or falsifier, residual risk or carrier restriction, including illegal alternatives rejected at construction, error codes, unreadable or missing inputs, and round-trips. Name the DESIGN item each line covers: its law id (for example law_version_identity or carrier_roundtrip), mutant id, or boundary/obligation name exactly as the DESIGN brief writes it. Ensure each obligation observable through the declared public port or an architecture or contract test at a DESIGN-declared locator has a test in the oracle set. An obligation the DESIGN assigns to a declared architecture or contract locator MUST be tested there, never reported NOT TESTED. Drive every test through the declared public port: build the stimulus and read the result through that port, never by importing production modules, constructing production objects, calling below the port or patching internal state, in test bodies or in support files. The only exception is an obligation the DESIGN places at a declared contract or architecture locator: there, construct only the members that DESIGN names for it, in one composition-root helper in the support files, and keep test bodies calling that helper; never use this exception to observe a public-port obligation below the port. Ask: "Which DESIGN obligations did you leave without a test because the main path already passes?" Leaving one untested for that reason is wrong. Also ask: "Which NOT TESTED line could a test at a DESIGN-declared locator observe after all?" Except for construction restrictions and error-code identities, which require the contract coverage or DESIGN rejection below, NOT TESTED is allowed only when neither the declared public port nor an architecture or contract test at a locator the DESIGN declares can observe the obligation; such an obligation does NOT make the assignment unconstructible. Write the oracle and supports for every observable obligation, report each permitted unreachable one as `O<n> [<DESIGN id or name>]: NOT TESTED - <reason from the DESIGN>; owner: <owner the DESIGN declares, or none declared>` (end the line with `owner: none declared` when the DESIGN declares no owner), and return `accepted`. Never invent a field, an operation or a fixture fact to reach it, never widen the driving surface, and never replace a production check. For a DESIGN prohibition on retries, recovery or additional discovery, observe the declared dependency interaction per public invocation; unchanged final output or file bytes alone do not establish that prohibition. For a DESIGN obligation that excludes a claim or preserves an output field, assert the excluded claim's absence and the field's presence explicitly; a positive label or a nullable lookup is not that observation.
- Test DESIGN-declared construction restrictions and error-code identities through their declared public contract surface: use the public port for emitted codes and observe accepted and refused inputs through the declared public port, using the injection seam where DESIGN declares one, in a contract test at the DESIGN-declared locator. Never mark these boundary obligations NOT TESTED. If no declared surface or locator can observe one, return `rejected` with `BLOCKED-BY design`, naming the obligation, the missing declaration and the DESIGN correction needed; do not import internals or invent a seam.
- Cover every DESIGN law with at least one Hypothesis @given property naming its exact id in the test name or docstring. For a finite domain, use st.sampled_from over the entire declared domain, including all alternatives and combinations, not a selected subset; retain tables for explicit examples, not as substitutes for the property. A full strategy domain is not evidence that every value was executed.
- Do not retain an incumbent test whose only assertion is that a command runs, returns a code, prints something or has a certain shape unless a DESIGN obligation names it. Test every named residual risk the DESIGN lists for this value, including combinations of two causes at once. A case the primary oracle test already observes is not repeated as a row of any example table, and a case held in a table does not get a separate test; keep a separate test only for a different assertion. Treat Hypothesis @example decorators and standalone finite examples as example-table cases: keep each explicit stimulus/assertion pair in one place across the primary oracle, finite tables and generated properties, retaining another occurrence only for a different assertion. Keep each concrete finite stimulus/assertion case once; when laws share it, one table observes it once and cites all applicable laws; each generative property adds only different cases or assertions.
- Name files, tests, titles and steps for user-visible behaviour in plain words; exclude value, slice, mandate, ADR and other process identifiers and production symbol names. Test names and docstrings state what the user observes in plain words; error-code constants, class names and function names of the production code never appear in them (only the DESIGN's own law and mutant identifiers may, so each test cites the law it checks).
- Write nothing meant for the examiner: no standalone runner, value selector or verbose mode in support files. Write each tested O line as `O<n> [<DESIGN id or name>]: stimulus <few words>; expected <few words>; user result <what the user can observe or accomplish, in plain words>; test <test file>::<test name>`, with no paths or argv in the stimulus, expected result or user result; write each untested O line as `O<n> [<DESIGN id or name>]: NOT TESTED - <reason from the DESIGN>; owner: <owner the DESIGN declares, or none declared>`. Every permitted NOT TESTED O line about a product limit, guarantee or restriction states the plain-word user result; keep pipeline, provenance and model-bound facts separate, with no user result required. The user result describes what the user observes; RED/GREEN/authored/collected state belongs only in the diagnostic summary's first lines, never as a user result or in an O line.
